From 0efb0b3a17198502d9d328d1ab6a5f12bfc8fbdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Carpio <jcarpio@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:37:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Tech front: Tech videos as a bottom row under the desks

Tech videos leaves the side column, where its large thumbnails made the
right column far taller than the rest of the front, and becomes the
front's last row under the desks, before "This week in Tech": a double
rule, thumbnails over their titles, three across, six across from 1920px
(TechQuery.VideosAsync already reads six). The side column keeps Just
released. Phones keep their own video rail.

New class tc-video-band (tc-video-row is the Tech desk pages' list row).
tech-front.browser.cjs: videos shown per width, no longer in the side
column, and below the desks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BeSUhVSrEYFW7YxEsPgtnC
